{"parentUuid":"3b48d3c3-bceb-414c-8ceb-c815d7a23bbe","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MHRuovP9N1XFSSoBmS62ZQ","type":"tool_result","content":"statement: >-\n  A compaction leaves a boundary in the transcript, followed by a summary and\n  a preserved tail of earlier records, so a reader can still follow the record\n  chain across it.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/claude-directory#application-data\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/compact\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/compact-nohooks\n  codex: pending\n  cursor: pending\ncommit f860ff366b50328d62a3ff06a1cd76d39e84245f\nAuthor: Mykyta Svyrydenko <<redacted-email>>\nDate:   Sat Oct 3 16:44:15 2026 +0200\n\n    codex: bash-tool-result cell supported, recorded in runs/shell-exit-status (#91)\n    \n    Codex tells the agent a failed command's output like a success's; the failure is only in the event stream's command_execution item (status failed, exit_code). Recorded with the real codex; the cell lists that as a deviation, and the mock does the same.\n    \n    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/shell_result_test.go      | 72 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n codex-mock/internal/events/stream.go               |  7 ++-\n .../snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/run.yaml      |  2 +\n .../shell-exit-status/samples/20261003-142833/SEAL |  6 ++\n .../samples/20261003-142833/events.jsonl           | 22 +++++++\n .../samples/20261003-142833/exit.txt               |  1 +\n .../samples/20261003-142833/payloads.jsonl         |  6 ++\n .../samples/20261003-142833/stderr.txt             |  1 +\n .../samples/20261003-142833/stream.jsonl           | 16 +++++\n ...8-34-01a1022a-acf2-7e12-9814-d1750d3ff095.jsonl | 28 +++++++++\n .../snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hook.sh |  5 ++\n .../runs/