ield, and the recorded PostToolUse payloads in runs/stops and runs/posttool-block contain no duration either, so either add a deviation for it or drop it from the statement.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, spec/capabilities/compaction-transcript-continuity.yaml (file-guard \"capability-grounded\")\n  - codex: the statement part 'Whatever the hook prints is not recorded in the transcript' is neither stated by the doc (hooks#sessionend only says 'their output won't steer Codex or keep the thread open', nothing about the transcript) nor shown by runs/session-end (its hook.sh prints nothing to stdout, only appends to $HOOK_LOG, so the sample cannot show printed output being absent from the transcript), and it is not listed in the cell's deviations.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, spec/capabilities/compaction-transcript-continuity.yaml (file-guard \"capability-grounded\")\n  - Codex is cited as supported with no deviations, but the statement says the Stop payload carries 'the background tasks still running'; the Codex doc's Stop table lists only turn_id, stop_hook_active and last_assistant_message, and the Stop payloads in codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops/samples/20261001-124319/payloads.jsonl have no background-task field, so that part needs to be listed as a codex deviation (or dropped from the statement).\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, spec/capabilities/compaction-transcript-continuity.yaml (file-guard \"capability-grounded\")\n  - Codex is cited as supported with no deviations, but the statement says the hook also fires for a background-task notification handed to the agent. Neither the codex UserPromptSubmit doc section (\"User prompt that's about to be sent\") nor the hook-exit-codes and prompt-blocked runs show or mention that. Both runs only fire the hook for the user-typed prompt. The claim needs a codex run or doc, or it has to be listed as a codex deviation.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, spec/capabilities/compaction-transcript-continuity.yaml (file-guard \"capability-grounded\")\n  - The Codex doc (hooks#matcher-patterns) says '*', '' or omitting matcher entirely each match every occurrence of an event. The recorded run covers '*' and '' but has no hook group without a matcher key. No test loads a hooks.json group with the matcher omitted (matcher_test.go's fired helper passes Matcher: '' directly), so the omitted-matcher variant is unchecked. Fix: add a group without a matcher to the hook-matchers run and assert that it fires.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/payloads.jsonl (and 19 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The only test marked sr:proves posttooluse-payload/codex (TestPostToolUsePayloadCarriesInputAndResponse, capabilities_test.go:285) drives one successful `echo FINE` call and checks tool_name, tool_input and tool_response. It does not check the other payload fields the recordings show (hook_event_name \"PostToolUse\", permission_mode \"bypassPermissions\", session_id). It does not check that the hook fires once per call, in order, across several calls, as posttool-block shows (POSTBLOCK, POSTBLOCK, AFTER). It also does not cover the doc statement at hooks#posttooluse that PostToolUse also runs after a Bash command that exits non-zero. A test for that exists in semantics_test.go but carries no sr:proves marker for this capability, so it does not count.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/payloads.jsonl (and 19 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The codex doc's Stop section says a matching Stop hook returning continue:false takes precedence over other hooks' block/continuation decisions, but no test drives that case. The only test, TestStopBlockContinuesTheTurnWithOneEnd, replays runs/stops. It checks three Stop events, that the rollout contains both reason strings, and one turn.completed. It never asserts that the agent produces further messages after a block. It does not exercise the hook-exit-codes variant of an exit-2 block with a custom stderr reason. It does not exercise Stop output that is plain text, which the doc calls invalid.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/payloads.jsonl (and 19 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestStopPayloadCarriesLastMessageAndContinuing asserts stops[0][last_assistant_message] == DONE, but none of the recorded Stop payloads in runs/stops contain that field (only session_id, hook_event_name, permission_mode, stop_hook_active); the doc-stated turn_id field is also not asserted by any test.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/payloads.jsonl (and 19 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The only test, TestUserPromptSubmitAddsContextOrRefuses, never covers the doc-stated block form (hooks#userpromptsubmit: JSON {\"decision\":\"block\",\"reason\":...} on stdout, besides exit 2), and the exit-2 case only asserts the stream shape [thread.started, turn.started, turn.completed]. That refusal check is too loose to catch the mock still running the prompt: it does not assert that echo SHOULDNOTRUN never ran, that no Stop hook fired (events.jsonl shows none), or that nothing reached the agent. The refusal case also has no test with an inline scenario where the hook sees the payload, and no test shows a hook cannot rewrite the prompt, for example by emitting a changed prompt and checking the agent still gets the original. The UserPromptSubmit JSON additionalContext form is checked only under hook-additional-context, not here.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity/samples/20261003-144854/payloads.jsonl (and 19 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - codex-mock/internal/runner/compact.go makes an undecided choice about what triggers auto-compaction in a mock. It has the mock estimate context size itself (`c.used += len(text) / 4` on every tool output, compacting once `c.used > c.limit`), while claude-mock triggers compaction from the scenario script (`{\"type\":\"compact\",\"trigger\":\"auto\"}` records) and spends no tokens. Neither the internal/compaction module (the sequence and what it preserves) nor any ADR decides whether the trigger is scripted or token-estimated, or how tokens are counted. No ADR decides this. Ask the user to decide it (a new ADR), or which existing ADR it falls under. Other items, all local or covered: the -c model_auto_compact_token_limit parse in exec.go (adr/mock-config), File.Record (module internal/transcript / session file), the window-chain record shape (compaction adapter, adr/capability-once), the test Args field (local). (file-guard \"concern-undeclared\")\n  - Home glob claude-mock/internal/runner/control*.go is too wide: control.go (handleControlRecord, worktree_create/worktree_remove/subagent_start hooks) belongs to the subagents/hooks concern, and control_fork.go (claudeForkSchema, forkSegment, preservedUUIDs) belongs to the session module's forking concern; narrow the glob to control_compact.go, control_boundary.go, control_frames.go, control_summary.go or move those files to their owning modules.\nThe files this refusal is about: internal/compaction/module.yaml (file-guard \"module-distinct\")\nexit 1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"59caacc9-069e-4d58-810d-fd24d48897bd","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:56:04.197Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1ac24f2e-0961-423c-af45-729e6008de9d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a7e54ea3099505a7e"}
