{"parentUuid":"f07799d0-14b1-45bb-98ff-014009917e7e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffbJXxnxhZn4BVF896Vk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The first sr-checks run refused my change, so I fixed what was mine and started a second run, which is still going. Nothing is pushed, there is no PR yet, and no check has passed.\n\n**Fixes after the first run**\n- **Compaction trigger moved into core.** The rule `capability-once` said the codex adapter was deciding when a compaction happens. The trigger (a token budget) now lives in the core as `internal/compaction/budget.go`. The codex mock only passes the limit and writes the `compacted` record.\n- **Module glob narrowed.** The compaction module's `claude-mock/internal/runner/control*.go` glob is now the four compaction files.\n- **No edit to `tool_host.go`.** The adapter hooks in through a new observer on the rollout file, so only `run.go` changes among the files that carry other capabilities' markers.\n- **Test helper renamed.** My `recordedRollout` collided with another agent's helper after the rebase, so it is now `compactionRollout`.\n- **Test results.** `go vet ./...` and `go test ./codex-mock/...` pass after the rebase.\n\n**What I expect the second run to still refuse**\n- **Unrelated refusals.** The first run's other refusals were about other capabilities' statements (hook-output, Stop payload, UserPromptSubmit, PostToolUse, matcher). They name my spec file, but the text is about codex cells I did not touch, so I think they are not mine. I'll report them rather than rewrite other capabilities.\n- **Possible `concern-undeclared` refusal.** It asked the user to decide, via an ADR, whether the mock's compaction trigger is scripted or token-estimated. The core `Budget` may not satisfy it, and I can't write that ADR without the user.\n\n**Cells, unchanged**\n- **codex: supported with two deviations.** Recorded in `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity`, with a `compacted` record chained by windows and a mock adapter and test.\n- **cursor: unsupported.** Recorded in `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity`, where headless `-p` has no compaction. I did not force a real context-overflow compaction in cursor.\n- **Old cursor binary.** I captured the cursor run with the 2026.09.28 binary, because `cursor-agent` auto-updated to 2026.10.01 and `capture.sh` refuses a version mismatch.\n\nNext, once the run is clean: push, open the PR, watch CI, and admin-merge only if every check passes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_read_input_tokens":184122,"output_tokens":848,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":757},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":848,"cache_read_input_tokens":184122,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":757,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffbJXhQiX42B6KaMy3r6","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b8d7457a-e2c9-4e80-9a85-91f64e147ab8","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:07:56.477Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b"}
