{"parentUuid":"c6901ebd-74ac-4d75-9ce2-c5ecda4a6347","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AoXiAyyJys5wrcYDmVzzSL","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - codex: the statement part 'Whatever the hook prints is not recorded in the transcript' is neither stated by the doc (hooks#sessionend only says 'their output won't steer Codex or keep the thread open', nothing about the transcript) nor shown by runs/session-end (its hook.sh prints nothing to stdout, only appends to $HOOK_LOG, so the sample cannot show printed output being absent from the transcript), and it is not listed in the cell's deviations.\n  - Codex is marked supported with no deviations, but the statement claims the Stop payload carries the background tasks still running. The Codex doc's Stop table lists only turn_id, stop_hook_active and last_assistant_message. The Stop payloads in codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops contain no background-tasks field. Add that part as a Codex deviation, or drop it from the statement.\n  - Codex is cited as fully supported with no deviations, but neither its doc (#userpromptsubmit, which only covers additionalContext and block/exit 2) nor its runs (hook-exit-codes, prompt-blocked) show the hook firing for a background-task notification or that a hook cannot rewrite the prompt; those parts must be grounded by a run or listed as deviations.\n  - The Codex doc (hooks#matcher-patterns) says '*', '' or omitting matcher entirely each match every occurrence of an event. The recorded run covers '*' and '' but has no hook group without a matcher key. No test loads a hooks.json group with the matcher omitted (matcher_test.go's fired helper passes Matcher: '' directly), so the omitted-matcher variant is unchecked. Fix: add a group without a matcher to the hook-matchers run and assert that it fires.\n  - The docs say PreToolUse and PostToolUse `additionalContext` is added as developer context, and that PostToolUse `continue: false` replaces the tool result with the hook's feedback. No sr:proves test for hook-output-transcript-records/codex covers any of the three. The PostToolUse `additionalContext` case appears only in capabilities_test.go, under hook-additional-context. `Interpret` and `readOutput` in decide.go do not handle `continue: false` for PostToolUse at all. The recorded runs and t\n  - The docs state that piped stdin is added as context to a prompt argument and that `codex exec -` reads the whole prompt from stdin (the 'Advanced stdin piping' section), but the mock never reads stdin (exec.go joins args only), no deviation declares this, and no test covers it. Also, every recorded stream (stops, hook-exit-codes, prompt-blocked) has two item.completed events with subtype error right after thread.started, and stops/hook-exit-codes have several intermediate agent_message items\n  - The existing tests match the recorded run (SessionEnd fires last with reason other, no model or permission_mode, hook output unrecorded, synchronous even when async, failures do not end the run abnormally). But the codex doc (hooks#sessionend) also says SessionEnd fires on archive/delete of an open conversation and after 30 minutes idle, and never runs for subagents. The mock models none of these, no test covers them, and session-end-hook.yaml declares no codex deviation for them. Add a code\n  - The Codex Stop doc says that when several matching Stop hooks run, `continue: false` from any one takes precedence over another hook's block/continuation decision. No test covers this and no deviation declares it: the mock's EndOfTurn (turn_host.go) returns on the first blocking hook and ignores `continue: false`. TestStopBlockContinuesTheTurnWithOneEnd also only checks that the reason text appears somewhere in the rollout. It does not check that the reason was handed back as a new user prom\n  - TestStopPayloadCarriesLastMessageAndContinuing only checks last_assistant_message == \"DONE\" and stop_hook_active false then true across two Stops; the doc's `last_assistant_message: string | null` (null when no assistant message is available) variant is never exercised, and the recorded third Stop (still stop_hook_active:true after a second block, per the stops sample) is not asserted by this capability's test.\n  - The codex test (TestUserPromptSubmitAddsContextOrRefuses) leaves several documented behaviours untested. (1) The refusal case only checks the stream shape [thread.started, turn.started, turn.completed] from a replay of the prompt-blocked recording. It never asserts that the agent did not run `echo SHOULDNOTRUN`, that no tool or PreToolUse event occurred, that stderr carried PROMPT-BLOCK-MSG, or that the prompt payload was logged. (2) The docs also describe blocking with JSON {\"decision\":\"blo\n  - The glob claude-mock/internal/runner/control*.go is too wide: control.go (handleControlRecord, worktree_create/worktree_remove/subagent_start control records) belongs to the subagents/hooks concerns, and control_fork.go (claudeForkSchema, forkSegment) belongs to the session concern (finding, resuming and forking a session); narrow the glob to control_compact.go, control_boundary.go, control_frames.go and control_summary.go, or move control.go and control_fork.go to their owning modules.\nexit 1\nexit 1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f90c004d-b318-4e62-aa8d-4d765a470a92","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:30:56.427Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c6901ebd-74ac-4d75-9ce2-c5ecda4a6347","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-adc1470310079e23b"}
