{"parentUuid":"736bb62c-5f91-42a4-a3b1-71a6132d0803","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BWBWXKjYjJh6bU3RMA9HvH","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - The doc (noninteractive#basic-usage, line 27) says codex exec streams progress to stderr and prints only the final agent message to stdout. TestExecWithoutJSONPrintsOnlyTheFinalMessage asserts only stdout. No test checks what stderr carries, and the mock writes nothing to stderr except tool-router errors. No deviation declares this either. The other doc and run items are covered: the JSONL event order and fields, the usage keys, failed command status, the single turn.completed, the prompt-blocked stream shape, and the -o/error/item-type deviations.\n  - The glob claude-mock/internal/runner/control*.go is too wide: control.go (handleControlRecord, worktree_create/worktree_remove/subagent_start control records) belongs to the subagents/hooks concern, and control_fork.go (claudeForkSchema, forkSegment) belongs to the session concern (forking a session); narrow the glob to control_compact.go, control_boundary.go, control_frames.go and control_summary.go, or move those files to their owning modules.\nexit 1\nexit 1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8f6a7831-e71d-4cae-bcbc-1e4f42c70435","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:59:31.479Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"736bb62c-5f91-42a4-a3b1-71a6132d0803","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a63bb90a3bc6561be"}
