{"parentUuid":"c376c49c-33e8-4c83-939b-22f2066a8e06","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfffHfHm5HJe6z64iX88H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fifth sr-checks run left two refusals, and I fixed one of them and started a sixth run, which is still going. Nothing is pushed yet, so there is no PR and no merge.\n\n- **Module glob (fixed).** The judge said `claude-mock/internal/runner/control*.go` was too wide for the compaction module. I narrowed it to the four compaction control files. I moved `control.go` into the hooks module and `control_fork.go` into the session module, so no file is left in no module.\n- **Pair on a marked declaration (named, not fixed).** The remaining refusal is about `noninteractive-run/codex`, a pair I touched by editing `Run` in `codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go` (one wiring line for the compaction observer). The judge says the doc has `codex exec` stream progress to stderr and print only the final message to stdout. The existing test asserts only stdout, and no deviation covers stderr. That gap is for the `noninteractive-run` debt agent, and the edit I made to `Run` is the only reason this pair was re-judged on my branch.\n\nIf that pair is the only refusal in the new run, I'll push, open the PR and watch CI. I'll admin-merge only if every check passes. If CI fails on that pair, I'll stop and report rather than merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":640,"cache_read_input_tokens":203273,"output_tokens":422,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":640},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":422,"cache_read_input_tokens