{"parentUuid":"f4b49b4d-90df-494d-95b7-29cdb55153f7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012gPZb8TkHo34okUssmVdbs","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - The doc (noninteractive#basic-usage, line 27) says codex exec streams progress to stderr and prints only the final agent message to stdout. TestExecWithoutJSONPrintsOnlyTheFinalMessage asserts only stdout. No test checks what stderr carries, and the mock writes nothing to stderr except tool-router errors. No deviation declares this either. The other doc and run items are covered: the JSONL event order and fields, the usage keys, failed command status, the single turn.completed, the prompt-blocked stream shape, and the -o/error/item-type deviations.\n  - The home glob claude-mock/internal/runner/control.go claims compaction code (defaultPreserved, compactionSpec, compactHookLines) that belongs to the compaction concern, which owns control_compact.go, control_boundary.go and related files. Move those compaction declarations into a compaction-owned file, leaving only handleControlRecord's hook firing in control.go, or narrow the glob.\n  - The home glob claude-mock/internal/runner/runner_session_hooks.go claims a file that fires SessionStart/SessionEnd hooks, extracts hook additionalContext and handles UserPromptSubmit blocking, which is the hooks module's concern (which handlers match an event, running them, what their result means), not finding/resuming/forking a session or giving it an id; move it to internal/hooks's home (or narrow this glob). The concern itself is distinct from the other modules.\n  - claude-mock/internal/runner/control_fork.go:10-14 and :26-38 (claudeForkSchema IsBoundary/IsSummary and preservedUUIDs) interpret the compact_boundary / isCompactSummary record shapes and parse compactMetadata.preservedMessages.uuids, which is the compaction module's knowledge of what a compaction preserves and duplicates the compactMetadata parsing in control_boundary.go:80-89; move this into the compaction home (e.g. a boundary/summary/preserved-uuid reader next to control_boundary.go/control_summary.go) and have the fork code call it. Other matches are fine: hooks/event.go:31-32 (EventP\nexit 1\nexit 1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"abe5ba17-0fec-43cf-8f99-1646b1c9099b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:05:55.333Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f4b49b4d-90df-494d-95b7-29cdb55153f7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b"}
