{"parentUuid":"bb3c2051-a7ae-4cf0-926f-e3a2efc57841","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfffk9vAbmMueNEra1zGQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not merged and not pushed: sr-checks still refuses this branch, and the `verify-before-push` gate blocks the push until it comes back clean. There is no PR.\n\nThe local branch `worktree-agent-aa43418fbebf671c6` is rebased on origin/main and builds. The last verified state (sr-checks run 5) had two refusals left, and neither is about my cells. The last commit is `1e9b2dc`.\n\n**Cells**\n- **codex: supported, with two deviations.** The real codex compacted after every tool call in `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity`. It writes one `compacted` record chained by window ids, with the kept prompt and an opaque summary. The mock writes the same record (`codex-mock/internal/runner/compact.go`). The trigger is a token budget in core (`internal/compaction/budget.go`). The test is `codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go`, and the frozen doc is `config-reference#configtoml`.\n- **cursor: unsupported.** Recorded in `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity`: `/summarize` under `-p` is plain text and no `preCompact` fires. I did not force a real context-overflow compaction in cursor. The run was captured with the 2026.09.28 binary through a PATH shim, because cursor-agent auto-updated to 2026.10.01 and `capture.sh` refuses the mismatch.\n\n**Remaining refusals**\n- **`noninteractive-run/codex`.** The doc says codex streams progress to stderr, and the existing stdout-only test and the missing deviation are what the judge objects to. My edit to `Run` in `codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go` (one wiring line) is why this pair was re-judged on my branch. This is the debt agent's to fix.\n- **Compaction module home glob.** The glob `claude-mock/internal/runner/control*.go` is too wide for the compaction module (`module-distinct`). I tried narrowing it and moving `control.go` and `control_fork.go` into the hooks and session modules. That only surfaced new refusals about `runner_session_hooks.go` and the fork code's compaction knowledge. I reverted to the original glob, so the refusal stands. This is claude-mock's existing module layout, not my change. It needs someone to split claude-mock's `control*.go` by concern.\n\nI made no ADR for the compaction trigger. The token budget in core did not draw a \"needs an ADR\" refusal in runs 5 and 6.\n\n**Decision for you:** choose one.\n- Authorise the push despite those two refusals.\n- Have a claude-mock refactor owner fix the module homes.\n- Have the `noninteractive-run` debt agent land first, then I rebase and re-run.\n\nI'll push, open the PR and merge as soon as sr-checks is clean."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":205717,"output_tokens":961,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":338},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":961,"cache_read_input_tokens":205717,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":338,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfffk97J1CiuVrFegT5sg","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"aa37df2b-759f-4529-a382-b3838fda3a49","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:06:11.695Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6