{"parentUuid":"5bcf5726-f09f-40f2-bccd-eb6c867242e7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffhBwDHVGzV4RjTHDVgq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J8QWF6h475iCUEJFrnKysJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -v \"cheap checks\" /private/tmp/claude-501/srchecks-ctc7.out | tail -2 | cut -c1-2500; ls adr/mock-config adr/modeled-surface; cat adr/mock-config/*.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":752,"cache_read_input_tokens":215105,"output_tokens":221,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":39},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":752},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":221,"cache_read_input_tokens":215105,"cache_creation_input_tokens":752,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":752,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01J8QWF6h475iCUEJFrnKysJ":{"command":"cd /Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6 && grep -v \"cheap checks\" /private/tmp/claude-501/srchecks-ctc7.out | tail -2 | cut -c1-2500; ls adr/mock-config adr/modeled-surface; cat adr/mock-config/*.md"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01J8QWF6h475iCUEJFrnKysJ":{"cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffhBvw9sHH2P61tsKK7V","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"706b7df5-3056-4250-b617-cd348f7bc3dd","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:25:03.836Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-ab2efb1b0554a0078"}
{"parentUuid":"706b7df5-3056-4250-b617-cd348f7bc3dd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J8QWF6h475iCUEJFrnKysJ","type":"tool_result","content":"internal/compaction/budget.go adds a core policy for how a mock counts tokens (`const CharsPerToken = 4`, `b.used += chars / CharsPerToken`, and auto-compaction fires once that estimate passes a limit), and codex-mock/internal/session/compact.go uses it to trigger compaction. That breaks with the rest of the project: claude-mock compaction is scripted by the scenario, with pre_tokens/post_tokens given explicitly, and elsewhere the rule is 'the mock spends no tokens, so they are 0' (events/stream.go, runner_resume.go, cursor frames). No ADR, and not the internal/compaction module's stated scope (the sequence and what it preserves), decides whether a mock estimates token usage, by what rule, or whether compaction is triggered by that estimate instead of by the scenario. Ask the user to decide it in a new ADR, or to say which existing ADR covers it. Checklist: exec.go -c parsing (covered by adr/mock-config); package-global `autoCompact` set by exec (local to codex-mock); File.Record and the compacted record shape (follows the recording, adr/capability-grounding); NewID reuse (module internal/session); test Args field (local); CharsPerToken estimate and token-budget trigger (undecided). (file-guard \"concern-undeclared\")\nexit 1\nadr/mock-config:\nADR.md\n\nadr/modeled-surface:\nADR.md\n---\nconcern: where a mock reads its configuration (flags and environment variables)\nsloprails: [file-guard/config-at-entry, file-guard/adr-conformance]\n# Files that still read or write the process environment themselves. The list\n# only shrinks.\nexceptions:\n  - claude-mock/internal/hooks/invoker_exec.go\n  - claude-mock/internal/hooks/plugin_cache.go\n  - claude-mock/internal/runner/agent.go\n  - claude-mock/internal/runner/background_bash.go\n  - claude-mock/internal/runner/runner_print.go\n  - claude-mock/internal/runner/session_paths.go\n  - claude-mock/internal/runner/stream.go\n  - claude-mock/internal/toolexec/toolexec_bash.go\n---\n\n# A mock reads its configuration once, at its entrypoint\n\n## Concern\n\nWhere a mock reads configuration: its command-line flags and the environment\nvariables it honours (for Claude Code, the harness's own variables such as\n`CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` and `CLAUDE_CODE_STOP_HOOK_BLOCK_CAP`, and the mock's\n`A10N_MOCK_*`).\n\n## Decision\n\n- A mock reads every flag and environment variable once, in its entrypoint\n  package (`<harness>-mock/*.go`), into one configuration value passed down.\n- No other code calls `os.Getenv`, `os.LookupEnv`, `os.Setenv`,\n  `os.Unsetenv` or `os.Environ`.\n- The names of the variables are the harness adapter's; what they control is\n  a field of the configuration.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6a03acf7-6c53-4878-8754-1faef9e9ee2f","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:25:05.779Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"706b7df5-3056-4250-b617-cd348f7bc3dd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-ab2efb1b0554a0078"}
