{"parentUuid":"76d15c8d-1df9-4e81-9bdd-fb681d5cfc5e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffhCZqRfX8Upj5ZTkU9K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RSHnRRJu8uzERk3uY9cL19","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6/adr/mock-compaction-trigger/ADR.md","content":"---\nconcern: what makes a mock compact its session on its own, and how it counts the context that triggers it\nsloprails: [file-guard/adr-conformance]\n---\n\n# A mock compacts on a scripted record, or on a token budget the run sets\n\n## Concern\n\nA real harness compacts a session by itself when its context passes a limit.\nA mock spends no tokens, so it has no context size of its own to pass a limit\nwith. What makes a mock compact, and how the size it compares is counted, must\nbe one rule, not one per harness.\n\n## Decision\n\n- A harness whose compaction the scenario can script (claude-mock's control\n  records, with their token counts given explicitly) compacts when the\n  scenario says so. The mock spends no tokens, so a count it is not given is 0.\n- A harness whose compaction is only the harness's own threshold (Codex's\n  `model_auto_compact_token_limit`) compacts on a token budget: the limit is\n  the run's setting, and what the context has grown by is estimated from the\n  text the agent was told, at `compaction.CharsPerToken` characters to the\n  token. The budget and the estimate live once, in `internal/compaction`; an\n  adapter passes the limit and writes the compaction in its harness's form.\n- The estimate is a modelled-surface deviation of the capability's cell: the\n  real harness counts the model's tokens.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":902,"cache_read_input_tokens":217140,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":902,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RSHnRRJu8uzERk3uY9cL19":{"file_path":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6/adr/mock-compaction-trigger/ADR.md","content":"---\nconcern: what makes a mock compact its session on its own, and how it counts the context that triggers it\nsloprails: [file-guard/adr-conformance]\n---\n\n# A mock compacts on a scripted record, or on a token budget the run sets\n\n## Concern\n\nA real harness compacts a session by itself when its context passes a limit.\nA mock spends no tokens, so it has no context size of its own to pass a limit\nwith. What makes a mock compact, and how the size it compares is counted, must\nbe one rule, not one per harness.\n\n## Decision\n\n- A harness whose compaction the scenario can script (claude-mock's control\n  records, with their token counts given explicitly) compacts when the\n  scenario says so. The mock spends no tokens, so a count it is not given is 0.\n- A harness whose compaction is only the harness's own threshold (Codex's\n  `model_auto_compact_token_limit`) compacts on a token budget: the limit is\n  the run's setting, and what the context has grown by is estimated from the\n  text the agent was told, at `compaction.CharsPerToken` characters to the\n  token. The budget and the estimate live once, in `internal/compaction`; an\n  adapter passes the limit and writes the compaction in its harness's form.\n- The estimate is a modelled-surface deviation of the capability's cell: the\n  real harness counts the model's tokens.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffhCZXKmFYTmSWkY5rpj","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"11cbc982-00c6-444e-a596-b4d663e0fbf0","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:25:15.804Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffo