{"parentUuid":"9e8f685f-bbc9-4831-8785-047d61230680","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffjQ7N3VTeqdNwzLELMQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The branch is still not pushed. sr-checks left two refusals that I can't fix cheaply or alone. There is no PR and nothing is merged. The local branch `worktree-agent-aa43418fbebf671c6` is rebased on origin/main and committed, and the tree is clean.\n\n**1. ADR: the two ADR judges want opposite things**\n- **The conflict.** `adr-grounded` wants `adr/mock-compaction-trigger/ADR.md` limited to what the user said (\"set a low token budget to reprodcue then\"). `adr-well-formed` wants it specific enough to check. It asks for the estimate formula, the code location, and which mocks compact on the budget versus on a scripted record.\n- **What I tried.** My fuller version was refused by `adr-grounded` as going beyond the quote. The trimmed version is now refused by `adr-well-formed`.\n- **What I need.** Either the user approves the more specific wording, or the coordinator tells me to reduce the ADR's claim.\n\n**2. cursor: the absence claim isn't demonstrated**\n- **What the recording shows.** My second recording (`cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity`) did not apply real pressure. Only one ~114KB part was read before `DONE`. There was no `preCompact` and the transcript has only plain user and assistant lines, but that shows nothing about a compaction.\n- **Why it can't be settled cheaply.** cursor-agent has no flag to set a compaction threshold, so only a very large run would settle it. Cursor's own hooks doc lists `preCompact`, so cursor does compact in some mode. I don't think \"unsupported\" can be shown honestly with a run this small.\n- **What I need.** Your call:\n  - Pay for a very large cursor recording.\n  - Mark cursor with a different cell shape.\n  - Leave the cursor cell unresolved, and have that go through the coordinator.\n\n**Everything else was clean in the last run.** That covers the codex cell, the mock adapter (`codex-mock/internal/session/compact.go`), the core budget (`internal/compaction/budget.go`), the test and the module rules.\n\nThe codex cell is supported with two deviations (capability-grounding, modeled-surface), recorded in `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity`. The cursor run was captured with the 2026.09.28 binary, because cursor-agent auto-updated and `capture.sh` refuses a version mismatch.\n\nIf you can settle those two points, I'll fix them, re-run sr-checks, push, open the PR, wait for CI and admin-merge once every check passes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":600,"cache_read_input_tokens":241469,"output_tokens":965,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":87},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":600},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":965,"cache_read_input_tokens":241469,"cache_creation_input_tokens":600,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":600,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffjQ6yE1VDwAGrLSUZSw","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c75d5593-876d-4188-bd0c-cc4415488083","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:54:08.120Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-adc1470310079e23b"}
{"parentUuid":"c75d5593-876d-4188-bd0c-cc4415488083","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"The coordinator sent a message while you were working:\nDecisions. (1) ADR: state the user's rule plus the mechanism already required by adr/capability-once, nothing new: \"A mock compacts a conversation when the token budget the run sets (Codex: model_auto_compact_token_limit, passed in at entry) is exceeded by the mock's running estimate of the conversation's size. The decision is core's: internal/compaction's Budget decides and an adapter only passes the configured limit and acts on the answer; a mock never compacts on size without a budget set.\" That is checkable (names Budget, the adapter's role, the flag) and adds no number or formula the user didn't choose; keep the user's quote trailer. If adr-grounded still objects to a specific clause, cut only that clause. (2) cursor: I authorise one larger recording: read big chunks via several shell calls until the context is well past 150k tokens of tool output (up to about 500k tokens total input; cursor-agent in `--model auto`; stop early if it shows compaction). If preCompact fires or the transcript shows a summary: make the cursor cell supported from what it shows (docs `https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#precompact` frozen + that run) and adapt/skip an adapter only if you can model it (otherwise modeled-surface deviation, the mock models no cursor compaction). If nothing compacts even then: cell unsupported with that run as the evidence and a one-line reason scoped to what it shows; accept the judge's verdict if it passes, and report if it still refuses.\n\nAddress this before completing your current task."},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"9073269d-c8c2-43c3-84b6-f879b3573537","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:57:26.992Z","origin":{"kind":"coordinator"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/slo