{"parentUuid":"3d48e88d-adb0-41c0-afe0-5d80fe52f427","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffkZi9RgHiA7oMNBUX9B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still not pushed, and there is no PR or merge. The last sr-checks run (13) is clean except for one refusal, `adr-well-formed` on `adr/mock-compaction-trigger/ADR.md`, and it is the conflict I flagged before.\n\nThe judge says the single Decision bullet \"names no package, file or mechanism\". It wants the code that owns the comparison named, the estimate defined, and the no-budget case stated.\n\nThose are the clauses `adr-grounded` rejected in run 12, because the user's words only cover \"a token budget the run sets\". So the two ADR judges can't both pass on the user's quote alone. The branch is committed and the tree is clean.\n\n**Decision for you:** either the user supplies more words (for example \"core owns the budget; adapters pass the limit; no budget means never compact\"), or we accept the ADR as it stands and treat its remaining refusal as a known gap.\n\nThe rest of run 13 was clean. The codex cell is supported with two deviations, recorded in `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity`. The cursor cell is unsupported, shown by the large recording where cursor compacted twice and left no boundary or summary record. It also cites the frozen `hooks#precompact` doc.\n\nThe cursor runs were captured with the 2026.09.28 binary, because cursor-agent auto-updated and `capture.sh` refuses a version mismatch.\n\nIf the user supplies the extra words, I add them to the ADR with that exact quote as the trailer, re-run sr-checks, push, open the PR and admin-merge once every check passes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351,"cache_read_input_tokens":254841,"output_tokens":575,"output_tokens_details":