{"parentUuid":"005b5b1f-a9a3-437e-9cb1-e194586939ab","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffmPcZf65Ns9fHeotwRz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made both changes in two separate commits, each with its verbatim trailer, and started a fourteenth sr-checks run, which is still going. Nothing is pushed yet, so there is no PR or merge.\n\n- **ADR (`adr/mock-compaction-trigger/ADR.md`):** it now says a mock compacts when the token budget the run sets is exceeded by its running estimate of the conversation's size. With no budget set, a mock never compacts on size. It says nothing about ownership.\n- **No-budget test:** `TestNoBudgetNeverCompactsOnSize` in `codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go` runs 100,000 lines of output with no budget and asserts no compaction record. It passes with the existing compaction test.\n- **Module (`internal/compaction/module.yaml`):** the `concern:` line now says core's `Budget` decides when a mock compacts on size and adapters only pass the configured limit and act on the answer. The home globs are untouched.\n\nIf the run is clean, I push, open the PR, watch CI and admin-merge once every check passes. If it refuses (`module-distinct` is the likeliest, since it judges every `module.yaml` change), I'll report the refusal and stop."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1070,"cache_read_input_tokens":258624,"output_tokens":408,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1070},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":408,"cache_read_input_tokens":258624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_toke