{"parentUuid":"11617af6-1735-476c-a569-f312a4dc7247","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffmhNki9TTTr329ZiPYe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still not pushed, and there is no PR or merge. The last sr-checks run (14) has two refusals left, and both are on files I changed to follow the user's decision. The local branch is committed and clean.\n\n1. **`adr-well-formed` on `adr/mock-compaction-trigger/ADR.md`.** The judge says the Decision \"names no package, function, config key or mechanism\". It wants `internal/compaction`'s `Budget` named, the place the budget enters, and the \"running estimate\" defined. The user put the `Budget` ownership in the module's concern line, not the ADR, so I can't add it to the ADR without more user words. In practice the judge's demand is exactly what the user ruled out of the ADR.\n\n2. **`module-distinct` on `internal/compaction/module.yaml`.** The judge says the home glob `claude-mock/internal/runner/control*.go` is too wide. It says `control.go` belongs to the subagents/hooks concerns and `control_fork.go` to session forking. This glob was already there. Any edit to this `module.yaml` re-judges it, and the coordinator told me to leave the globs untouched. Earlier attempts to narrow it surfaced other module refusals in claude-mock, so I reverted them.\n\nThe rest of run 14 was clean:\n- **codex cell:** supported, with two deviations (capability-grounding, modeled-surface), recorded in `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/compaction-transcript-continuity`. The adapter is `codex-mock/internal/session/compact.go`, the core budget is `internal/compaction/budget.go`, and there is a no-budget e2e test.\n- **cursor cell:** unsupported. In the recording, cursor compacted twice and left no boundary or summary record. The cell also cites the frozen `hooks#precompact` doc.\n- **cursor capture binary:** the cursor run was captured with the 2026.09.28 binary, because cursor-agent auto-updated and `capture.sh` refuses a version mismatch.\n\n**Decision for you:** choose one.\n- (a) Allow the ADR to name `internal/compaction`'s `Budget`, with the user's approval.\n- (b) Have the claude-mock `control*.go` files split by concern, so the compaction glob can be narrowed.\n- (c) Authorise pushing despite these two judge refusals.\n\nWith (a) and (b) I re-run sr-checks, push, open the PR and admin-merge once every check passes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":638,"cache_read_input_tokens":260589,"output_tokens":939,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":129},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":638},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":939,"cache_read_input_tokens":260589,"cache_creation_input_tokens":638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":638,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffmhNN9F3t4UeMQwqsK7","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"82737782-ac7e-491e-8a5e-7a38283ab29b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:24:15.533Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b"}
{"parentUuid":"82737782-ac7e-491e-8a5e-7a38283ab29b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"aa43418fbebf671c6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"The coordinator sent a message while you were working:\n(1) Rebase onto origin/main first: PR #123 (manual-compaction) already moved claude's control.go/control_fork.go between modules and rewrote the compaction module's homes, so the wide-glob module-distinct refusal may be gone; check internal/compaction/module.yaml on main and re-apply only your concern-line edit (keep home globs exactly as main has them; if your branch needs a new home entry, add only that). (2) ADR: you may name the mechanism the user's rule already implies without adding ownership or formulas: the config key and the pinning test. Wording: \"A mock compacts a conversation when the run sets a token budget (codex-mock: `-c model_auto_compact_token_limit=<n>`) and the mock's running estimate of the conversation's size exceeds it; with no budget set a mock never compacts on size (codex-mock/e2e TestNoBudgetNeverCompactsOnSize pins it).\" Do not name Budget/ownership in the ADR. Keep the user's trailer for the commit that changes the ADR. If adr-well-formed still insists on more after that, accept it: report the exact finding and push anyway is NOT allowed; instead tell me and I'll ask the user once more.\n\nAddress this before completing your current task."},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"cf3403ee-e604-4136-b0dc-3e3b116396be","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:29:38.483Z","origin":{"kind":"coordinator"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-aa43418fbebf671c6","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b"}
